pra: 0201 - instrument the digitizer host-state and display-power interfaces

Provenance: backboardd's own persisted log from the T21a boot (the 10.4 MB
Persist/0000000000000001.tracev3 read out in
work/digitizer-gate-2026-11-22.md section 0) says the digitizer is matched and
alive - a BKIOHIDService "Status: matched" record, a BKDigitizerStreamClient -
and at the same time the winning BKSHIDUISensorMode (SpringBoard's, score 4108
against backboardd's baseline 1) carries digitizerEnabled: NO with
display: off, and its multitouchHostStateKeys list (WakeOnTap...) names a
contract this port never advertises and never accepts: SweetHIDTouch publishes
DisplayIntegrated/SurfaceWidth/SurfaceHeight and nothing else,
IOHIDEventService::setElementValue returns kIOReturnUnsupported, setProperties
returns success while doing nothing, and no digitizer event has ever carried
kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerIsDisplayIntegrated. The blank behind display: off is
BacklightServices' own "idle timer" transition, i.e. the normal sleep mode, and
it only costs the taps that arrive while it is latched. On the other hand the
panel is provably lit while userland believes it is off: `grep -c
'display-off request ignored (keep_on)'` gives 2 (ring62), 2 (ring63), 0
(ring60), 0 (ring61), and none of those four rings contains a single
`notifications type` or `sel 72` line (grep -c, 0 each) - no client has ever
registered a framebuffer notification, so the kernel's only display-state
output is the vsync.

BASE: the old side of this patch is the post-0171 state of
iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp and the post-0200 state of
iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp. Only 0150, 0171 and this patch touch the
framebuffer file, and `patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --dry-run` of both 0150 and 0171
against xnu-src/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp answers "previously
applied", so that working-tree copy IS the CI state after 0171; the HID side is
work/0200/SweetHID-post0200.cpp (cmp rc=0). Durable copies
work/0201/SweetFramebuffer-pre0201.cpp and -post0201.cpp were re-derived from
those exact bases and this patch re-applies to them with fuzz=0 and cmp rc=0
for both files (an earlier copy of the framebuffer file came from a different
base and was discarded - it carried a prague_gpu_present_slot block that the
CI tree does not have at this point in the stack).

Every guess about that split is currently unfalsifiable in a ring, so this patch
changes no behaviour - nothing is accepted, applied or delivered differently -
and only makes the three interfaces observable:

 1. display power: log EVERY kSweetFBRequestPowerChange call with the raw
    argument, the derived off, whether keep_on swallowed it and whether the
    request differs from the current state; record the request in fUserlandOff
    even when keep_on refuses it; and log each frame presented while
    fUserlandOff is set (present() is bounded to 26,000,000/10 = 2,600,000
    ticks = 0.1 s = 10 Hz by fMinGap, python3: 26000000//10 -> 2600000,
    (26000000//10)/26000000 -> 0.1).
 2. notification registration: log every kSweetFBNotifications call with its
    type and function pointer - today only a once-per-selector line exists,
    behind a guard that hides repeats.
 3. host state: log the refused setElementValue calls (return value unchanged)
    and the keys pushed through setProperties (8 per call), and mark our
    digitizer events display-integrated on the collection and on every finger
    child, logged once per boot. This last item is the only one that touches
    what userland sees; it is the final two hunks of SweetHID.cpp and both new
    lines carry the 0201 (7) marker, so a bisect can drop item 7 alone.

Ring lines that prove the gate moved (next boot, work/ring64-full.txt):

    SWEET HID: SweetHIDTouch setElementValue page 0x.. usage 0x.. ->
        backboardd IS pushing host state.
    SWEET HID: SweetHIDTouch setProperties key ..
        backboardd IS pushing properties.
    SWEET FB: powerreq n=2 arg=0 off=1 keep=1 applied=1
        a second, refused display-off request - visible instead of silent.
    SWEET FB: swap N while userland-display-off
        frames presented into a state userland calls "off".

Ring lines that falsify it:

  - No setElementValue and no setProperties line in the whole boot: backboardd
    never configures the digitizer through the event service, so 0202 is the
    wrong lever and the gate is downstream (SpringBoard routing) - stop there
    and do the tracev3 decode instead.
  - powerreq shows arg=1 only (no off=1) in a boot whose sensor-mode records
    still say displayState: off: the blank is entirely BLS-side, the framebuffer
    is not even consulted, the display-state lever is dead and only the
    host-state/wake path (0202) remains.
  - notifyreg lines appear with a type != 5: someone does subscribe to display
    notifications, so implementing them (0203) becomes cheap and testable; their
    absence keeps 0203 speculative.

FALSIFIER: expect per boot 1-2 `SWEET FB: powerreq n=<k> arg=0 off=1 keep=1
applied=<0|1>` lines (ring62 and ring63 each hold exactly 2 refused off
requests), 0.. a few `SWEET FB: notifyreg type <t> func 0x<f>` lines, and - only
if backboardd pushes host state during the harvest - `SWEET HID: SweetHIDTouch
setElementValue ...` / `setProperties key ...` lines. `SWEET HID: digitizer
events marked display-integrated` must appear at most once per boot, before the
first `SWEET HID: touch N down`. A boot that still logs `A5XELTE FB: display-off
request ignored (keep_on)` but has zero `SWEET FB: powerreq` lines is impossible
(both live in the same case arm) and means this patch did not land.

